<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Isly</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1844</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franco-moroccan-war">Franco-Moroccan War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Isly was fought on 14 August 1844 near the Isly river, close to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oujda">Oujda</a> in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a>, between a French army under Marshal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thomas-robert-bugeaud">Thomas-Robert Bugeaud</a> and a much larger Moroccan force led by the sultan's son. The French victory ended Morocco's support for Abd al-Qadir's resistance in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeria">Algeria</a> and exposed the weakness of the Moroccan army, opening the country to growing European pressure.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-isly.jpg" alt="Battle of Isly" width="320" height="154" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Horace Vernet · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vernet_-_Bataille_d%27Isly_-_1846.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
